-- casinovasgaming-leaderboard-guide
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Casinova Leaderboard Guide: How Rankings Are Calculated$t$,
  excerpt = $t$The Casinova Gaming leaderboard ranks the top 50 members by total VIP points, highest first. It is one all-time board: there are no daily, weekly or monthly resets and no prize attached to a position. Points come from card deposits, daily check-ins, the daily spin, completed game account requests and referrals.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>The Casinova Gaming leaderboard ranks the top 50 members by total VIP points, highest first. It is one all-time board: there are no daily, weekly or monthly resets and no prize attached to a position. Points come from card deposits, daily check-ins, the daily spin, completed game account requests and referrals.</p>

<h2>What the leaderboard shows</h2>
<p>The <a href="/leaderboard">leaderboard page</a> is public, so you can read it without logging in. It is a single table with four columns:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Rank.</strong> Position 1 to 50, ordered by VIP points from highest to lowest.</li>
<li><strong>Player.</strong> A shortened version of the member's name (see below).</li>
<li><strong>Tier.</strong> Bronze, Silver, Gold or Platinum.</li>
<li><strong>VIP Points.</strong> The member's lifetime points total.</li>
</ul>
<p>Only the top 50 accounts are listed. Suspended accounts are left off. The page is rebuilt roughly every two minutes, so a change in your points can take a couple of minutes to appear. If no rankings are available yet, the page shows "Rankings will appear soon" in place of the table.</p>

<h2>How rankings are calculated</h2>
<p>There is no separate leaderboard score. Your rank is your VIP points total compared with everyone else's. The same number decides your VIP tier, which is why the board also works as a quick way to see how far the next tier is in practice. These are the actions that add points:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>VIP points</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Card deposit credited to your wallet</td><td>1 point per dollar, rounded to the nearest whole point</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily check-in on the Daily rewards page</td><td>5 on the first day, 1 more for each consecutive day, up to 11 from day seven</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily mission: spin the wheel, then claim</td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cash prize on the daily spin</td><td>10 points per dollar won, so 10 to 100</td></tr>
<tr><td>Game account request completed by staff</td><td>50</td></tr>
<tr><td>Friend signs up with your referral code</td><td>10</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The check-in streak follows the calendar day in UTC. Miss a day and the streak starts again at 5 points. Points do not expire and the board never resets, so the total only moves up.</p>

<h2>How your name appears</h2>
<p>The board never shows a full name or an email address. If your profile has a first and last name, it shows the first name and the initial of the last name, for example "Maria L.". If your profile has one name only, it shows the first letter followed by asterisks. If there is no name on the profile, it shows the first two characters of your email followed by asterisks. There is no opt-in step: any active account with enough points to reach the top 50 is listed automatically.</p>

<h2>What the leaderboard is not</h2>
<p>An older version of this guide described things the site does not have. To be clear:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>No period boards.</strong> There is no daily, weekly or monthly board. One all-time table only.</li>
<li><strong>No XP.</strong> The board counts VIP points. Casinova has no XP or level number; the <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-xp-leveling-explained">XP and levels guide</a> explains what exists instead.</li>
<li><strong>No prize for placing.</strong> Finishing first, or in the top ten, pays nothing extra. The benefits come from your tier, not your rank.</li>
<li><strong>No effect on games.</strong> Rank does not change the deposit match, the $5 to $500 load range or the redeem rules, and it has no influence on results inside a game.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How rank relates to VIP tiers</h2>
<p>Because the board and the tiers use the same number, the tier column tells you roughly where the thresholds sit on the table: Bronze from 0 points, Silver from 500, Gold from 2,000 and Platinum from 5,000. What a tier changes is your referral share of a friend's first deposit (5%, 10%, 15%, 25%) and your daily spins (1, 2, 3, 3). The <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-vip-tiers-explained">VIP tiers guide</a> has the full table, and the <a href="/vip">VIP page</a> shows your own points when you are logged in.</p>

<h2>Sensible ways to move up</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check in every day.</strong> Open Daily rewards in your dashboard and claim. A full week of consecutive check-ins is 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 and 11 points, 56 in total, and every day after that is 11 as long as the streak holds.</li>
<li><strong>Spin, then claim the mission.</strong> Take your <a href="/spin">daily spin</a>, then go back to Daily rewards and claim the 5 mission points. A cash prize on the wheel adds 10 points per dollar on top. The <a href="/blog/daily-rewards-coins-guide">daily spin guide</a> lists the prizes.</li>
<li><strong>Refer people who will actually use the site.</strong> Each sign-up with your code is 10 points. The <a href="/blog/referral-program-earn-coins">referral guide</a> covers the code and the first-deposit share.</li>
<li><strong>Let deposits count, but do not deposit for rank.</strong> A $50 card deposit adds 50 points. That is a side effect of money you already planned to play with, not a reason to add more.</li>
</ol>
<p>That last point matters. A leaderboard position has no cash value, and points earned by depositing more than you intended are expensive points. Set your budget first and treat rank as a by-product. If keeping up with the board starts to shape how much you spend, the <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a> has tools and contacts.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Do I need to opt in to appear on the leaderboard?</h3>
<p>No. The board lists the 50 active accounts with the most VIP points automatically, with names shortened so no full name or email is shown.</p>
<h3>Does the leaderboard reset?</h3>
<p>No. It is a single all-time ranking by total VIP points. There are no daily, weekly or monthly boards.</p>
<h3>Is there a prize for finishing first?</h3>
<p>No. Rank itself pays nothing. The practical benefits, a higher referral share and more daily spins, come from your VIP tier.</p>
<h3>Why am I not on the board?</h3>
<p>Only the top 50 accounts by points are shown. Your own points total and the gap to the next tier are on the VIP page in your dashboard.</p>
<h3>How quickly does the board update?</h3>
<p>The page is refreshed about every two minutes, so new points can take a short while to show.</p>

<p><a href="/register?src=blog_casinovasgaming-leaderboard-guide&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=casinovasgaming-leaderboard-guide">Create your free account</a> and your points start counting from your first check-in.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is for players 18+. Sweepstakes availability varies by jurisdiction; void where prohibited.</p>$t$,
  seo_title = $t$Casinova Leaderboard: How Rankings Are Calculated$t$,
  seo_description = $t$The Casinova leaderboard ranks the top 50 members by total VIP points. One all-time board, no resets, no prizes. See how points are earned.$t$,
  tags = ARRAY[$t$casinovasgaming leaderboard$t$, $t$leaderboard rewards$t$, $t$vip points$t$]::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'casinovasgaming-leaderboard-guide' AND status = 'published';

-- casinovasgaming-next-generation-gaming-platform
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Casinova Gaming: How the Platform Works, End to End$t$,
  excerpt = $t$Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes gaming platform that puts one account and one wallet in front of eight third-party game apps, including Juwa, Game Vault and Vegas Sweeps. You deposit by card, load $5 to $500 into a game, and redeem from the game panel once the balance reaches 3x the load. It is not a licensed casino, and availability varies by jurisdiction.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes gaming platform that puts one account and one wallet in front of eight third-party game apps, including Juwa, Game Vault and Vegas Sweeps. You deposit by card, load $5 to $500 into a game, and redeem from the game panel once the balance reaches 3x the load. It is not a licensed casino, and availability varies by jurisdiction.</p>

<h2>What "platform" means here</h2>
<p>The games themselves are made by outside providers. Each one normally needs its own login and its own way of adding credits. Casinova sits in front of them: you hold one Casinova account, one wallet, and a panel for each game where you create a login, load credits, check the balance and submit a redeem. Your deposit history, VIP points and support messages stay in the same account no matter which game you open.</p>

<h2>What is inside a Casinova account</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>A wallet.</strong> Funded by card through a payment partner. Checkout happens on the partner's page.</li>
<li><strong>A panel per game.</strong> Create the game login, load, check balance and redeem from one screen.</li>
<li><strong>A daily spin.</strong> A free wheel with prizes of $1, $2, $3, $4, $7 or $10, or nothing. Bronze members get 1 spin per 24 hours, Silver 2, Gold and Platinum 3. See the <a href="/blog/daily-rewards-coins-guide">daily spin guide</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Daily rewards.</strong> A check-in that adds VIP points, with a streak that raises the daily amount.</li>
<li><strong>VIP tiers.</strong> Bronze, Silver, Gold and Platinum at 0, 500, 2,000 and 5,000 points. Explained in the <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-vip-tiers-explained">VIP tiers guide</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Referrals.</strong> A personal code. You receive 5% to 25% of a referred friend's first deposit, depending on your tier, plus 10 VIP points.</li>
<li><strong>A leaderboard.</strong> The top 50 members by VIP points, on the public <a href="/leaderboard">leaderboard page</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Support chat.</strong> A chat bubble on the site and a Messages inbox in the dashboard, available around the clock.</li>
<li><strong>ID verification.</strong> An upload page for a government ID, required before any redeem.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How it works, end to end</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Create a free account</strong> and verify your email.</li>
<li><strong>Deposit by card.</strong> The <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">deposit guide</a> walks through checkout. Card is the only method. Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime and crypto are not offered.</li>
<li><strong>Open a live game and create your game login</strong> from its panel. The login appears in the panel when it is ready.</li>
<li><strong>Load credits.</strong> Any whole-dollar amount from $5 to $500 per load. The deposit match is applied at this step. Details in <a href="/blog/how-to-load-credits-from-wallet">how to load credits</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Play</strong> in the provider's app or web player with the login from your panel.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem.</strong> When the in-game balance reaches 3x your load, submit a redeem from the same panel. You need an approved ID, and staff review every request. See <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">how to redeem</a>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>The money rules in one table</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>What applies</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Deposit method</td><td>Card only, through a payment partner</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deposit match</td><td>100% on the first deposit, 50% on the second, none after</td></tr>
<tr><td>When the match is applied</td><td>When you load a game</td></tr>
<tr><td>Load size</td><td>$5 minimum, $500 maximum, rounded to the nearest dollar</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem threshold</td><td>In-game balance of at least 3x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem cap</td><td>8x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem requirements</td><td>Approved government ID and a staff review</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The same rules apply to every live game and every VIP tier. There is no payout-time promise: a redeem is finished when the review is finished.</p>

<h2>Games you can load now</h2>
<p>Eight games are live: <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a>, <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a>, <a href="/games/mr-all-in-one">MR All In One</a>, <a href="/games/cash-machine">Cash Machine</a>, <a href="/games/cash-frenzy">Cash Frenzy</a>, <a href="/games/vegas-sweeps">Vegas Sweeps</a>, <a href="/games/gameroom">Gameroom</a> and <a href="/games/mafia">Mafia</a>. Between them they cover slots, keno and fish shooters. If you are unsure where to start, the <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-a-fish-table-game">four-question guide</a> narrows it down.</p>
<p>Six more titles are listed as coming soon and cannot be loaded yet: Orion Stars, Fire Kirin, Panda Master, Vblink, Milky Way and Ultrapanda. Their cards on the games page carry a "soon" badge. The <a href="/blog/fire-kirin-orion-stars-alternatives">coming-soon guide</a> suggests the closest live game for each.</p>

<h2>What the platform does not do</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>It does not set game outcomes.</strong> Results come from each provider's software and are based on chance. Casinova does not publish odds or RTP because the providers do not.</li>
<li><strong>It does not offer promo codes, free credits or a no-deposit bonus.</strong> The deposit match and the daily spin are the offers.</li>
<li><strong>It does not take payment outside card checkout.</strong> Anyone asking you to send money another way in Casinova's name is not Casinova.</li>
<li><strong>It does not claim to be available everywhere.</strong> Sweepstakes rules differ by jurisdiction, and checking yours is your responsibility.</li>
</ul>
<p>Play is for adults 18 and over. Decide what you can afford before you deposit, and use the <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a> if it stops being fun.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Is Casinova Gaming a casino?</h3>
<p>No. It is a sweepstakes gaming platform, not a licensed casino. Availability varies by jurisdiction.</p>
<h3>How do I deposit?</h3>
<p>By card, through the payment partner's checkout page. No other payment method is offered.</p>
<h3>Which games are available right now?</h3>
<p>Game Vault, Juwa, MR All In One, Cash Machine, Cash Frenzy, Vegas Sweeps, Gameroom and Mafia. Games marked coming soon cannot be loaded yet.</p>
<h3>What do I need before I can redeem?</h3>
<p>An in-game balance of at least 3x your load and an approved government ID. Staff review each request, and total redeems are capped at 8x the load.</p>
<h3>Do I need a separate wallet for each game?</h3>
<p>No. One Casinova wallet funds every live game. Each game has its own login and balance once you load it.</p>

<p><a href="/register?src=blog_casinovasgaming-next-generation-gaming-platform&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=casinovasgaming-next-generation-gaming-platform">Create your free account</a> and look around the dashboard before you deposit anything.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is for players 18+. Sweepstakes availability varies by jurisdiction; void where prohibited.</p>$t$,
  seo_title = $t$How the Casinova Gaming Platform Works$t$,
  seo_description = $t$One account and one card-funded wallet for eight live sweepstakes games. Loads from $5 to $500, 100% then 50% match, redeem at 3x with ID review.$t$,
  tags = ARRAY[$t$casinovasgaming$t$, $t$gaming platform$t$, $t$how to deposit$t$, $t$sweepstakes$t$, $t$getting started$t$]::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'casinovasgaming-next-generation-gaming-platform' AND status = 'published';

-- casinovasgaming-telegram-support-guide
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Casinova Gaming Telegram and Support: How to Get Help$t$,
  excerpt = $t$Casinova Gaming has an official Telegram at t.me/casinovagaming, linked from the footer of every page, and it is where promotions and new guides are announced. Account support itself runs through the live chat on the site and the Messages inbox in your dashboard, 24/7. For anything about a deposit, a game login or a redeem, use the site chat, where staff can see your account.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>Casinova Gaming has an official Telegram at t.me/casinovagaming, linked from the footer of every page, and it is where promotions and new guides are announced. Account support itself runs through the live chat on the site and the Messages inbox in your dashboard, 24/7. For anything about a deposit, a game login or a redeem, use the site chat, where staff can see your account.</p>

<h2>What the Telegram is for</h2>
<p>The Telegram link sits with the other social icons in the site footer. Casinova uses Telegram to post promotion alerts and links to new blog guides, so following it is a convenient way to hear about a new card on the <a href="/promotions">promotions page</a> without checking the site every day.</p>
<p>It is not connected to your account. Nothing you send on Telegram is attached to your wallet, your game panels or your ID status, and you do not need a Telegram account to use Casinova at all.</p>

<h2>Where support actually happens</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Who it is for</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Chat bubble on the site</td><td>Visitors who are not logged in</td><td>General questions before you sign up</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chat and Messages in the dashboard</td><td>Logged-in members</td><td>Deposits, game logins, loads, redeems, ID verification</td></tr>
<tr><td>Telegram</td><td>Anyone</td><td>Promotion alerts and new guides</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The <a href="/support">support page</a> lists the same options along with common questions.</p>

<h2>How the dashboard chat works</h2>
<p>When you are logged in, the chat has two modes, shown as two tabs at the top of the window:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>AI Assistant.</strong> The default. It answers common questions straight away, such as the load range or how redeem works.</li>
<li><strong>Real Agent.</strong> Tap this tab to hand the conversation to a person. The chat shows a notice that an agent has been notified and will reply in the same window.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is the real link between Casinova support and Telegram: when you message support and no agent is online on the site, the team receives an alert on their own internal Telegram so someone can pick it up. You do not need to do anything on Telegram for that to happen, and the reply arrives in the site chat, not on Telegram.</p>
<p>The Messages inbox also accepts attachments, so you can send a screenshot of what you are seeing. Your conversation history stays in the inbox, which gives you a written record if you need to refer back to it.</p>

<h2>What to include so the first reply is useful</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>The game.</strong> For example <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a> or <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a>.</li>
<li><strong>What you did and when.</strong> "Loaded $20 at about 3 pm" is far more useful than "my load is missing".</li>
<li><strong>What the panel shows now.</strong> A screenshot of the game panel or your deposit history saves a round of questions.</li>
<li><strong>What you expected.</strong> One sentence is enough.</li>
</ol>
<p>Many questions are answered faster by a guide than by a queue. For a deposit that has not appeared, read the <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">card deposit guide</a>. For a locked redeem, check <a href="/blog/casinova-id-verification-guide">ID verification</a> and <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">how to redeem</a> first, because the usual causes are an ID still in review or a balance below 3x the load.</p>

<h2>Staying safe on Telegram</h2>
<p>Telegram makes it easy for anyone to create an account with a familiar name and logo. Treat every direct message that claims to be Casinova with suspicion, and keep these rules:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use the link in the site footer.</strong> The official handle is t.me/casinovagaming. Do not trust a handle sent to you by a stranger.</li>
<li><strong>Card checkout on the site is the only way to deposit.</strong> Casinova does not take Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime or crypto, so a request to pay that way is not from Casinova.</li>
<li><strong>Never share your password, a login code or your full card number</strong> in any chat.</li>
<li><strong>Upload your ID only in the dashboard.</strong> The ID verification page is the place for it, not a Telegram chat.</li>
<li><strong>Ignore offers of promo codes or free credits.</strong> Casinova has no promo codes and no free credits, so a message offering them is bait.</li>
</ul>
<p>The <a href="/blog/is-casinovasgaming-legit">guide to checking whether Casinova is legit</a> covers what else you can verify yourself.</p>

<h2>Does VIP tier change support?</h2>
<p>The VIP page lists standard support at Bronze, priority support at Silver, 24/7 VIP support at Gold and a dedicated account manager at Platinum. All of it happens through the same site chat and Messages inbox. There is no separate Telegram line for higher tiers, and Casinova does not publish a response-time figure for any tier. The <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-vip-tiers-explained">VIP tiers guide</a> lists the thresholds.</p>
<p>If you are contacting support because play has become stressful or you want a break, say so directly, and see the <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a>.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Is Telegram the way to contact Casinova support?</h3>
<p>No. Support runs through the live chat on the site and the Messages inbox in your dashboard. Telegram is used for promotion alerts and new guides.</p>
<h3>Do I need a Telegram account to use Casinova?</h3>
<p>No. Everything, including deposits, loads, redeems and support, works on the site without Telegram.</p>
<h3>What is the official Casinova Telegram?</h3>
<p>t.me/casinovagaming, which is the link behind the Telegram icon in the site footer.</p>
<h3>Someone on Telegram asked me to pay by Cash App or crypto. Is that Casinova?</h3>
<p>No. Deposits are by card through the checkout on the site and no other method is offered. Do not send money, and report the account to support through the site chat.</p>
<h3>How do I reach a person instead of the AI assistant?</h3>
<p>Log in, open the chat and tap the Real Agent tab. An agent is notified and replies in the same chat window.</p>

<p><a href="/register?src=blog_casinovasgaming-telegram-support-guide&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=casinovasgaming-telegram-support-guide">Create your free account</a> and you will find the chat in your dashboard from the first login.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is for players 18+. Sweepstakes availability varies by jurisdiction; void where prohibited.</p>$t$,
  seo_title = $t$Casinova Telegram and Support: How to Get Help$t$,
  seo_description = $t$The official Casinova Telegram posts promotions and guides. Account support runs through the site's live chat and dashboard Messages, 24/7.$t$,
  tags = ARRAY[$t$casinovasgaming telegram support$t$, $t$casinovasgaming contact$t$]::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'casinovasgaming-telegram-support-guide' AND status = 'published';

-- casinovasgaming-vs-online-casinos
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Casinova Gaming vs Online Casinos: What Is the Difference?$t$,
  excerpt = $t$Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes gaming platform, not a licensed online casino. A licensed casino holds a gambling license from a regulator and operates only where that license applies; Casinova holds no casino license, makes no claim about where it is legal, and its availability varies by jurisdiction. In practice the differences you will notice are how you pay, how you redeem and what information is published about the games.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes gaming platform, not a licensed online casino. A licensed casino holds a gambling license from a regulator and operates only where that license applies; Casinova holds no casino license, makes no claim about where it is legal, and its availability varies by jurisdiction. In practice the differences you will notice are how you pay, how you redeem and what information is published about the games.</p>

<h2>Quick comparison</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th></th><th>Casinova Gaming</th><th>Licensed online casino (in general)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Legal basis</td><td>Sweepstakes model, no casino license</td><td>Gambling license issued by a regulator</td></tr>
<tr><td>Where it operates</td><td>Varies by jurisdiction; you must check your own</td><td>Only in places covered by its license</td></tr>
<tr><td>Games</td><td>Third-party apps such as Juwa and Game Vault, each with its own login</td><td>Games offered inside the casino's own site or app</td></tr>
<tr><td>Paying in</td><td>Card only, through a payment partner</td><td>Depends on the operator</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bonus</td><td>100% match on the first deposit, 50% on the second, none after</td><td>Depends on the operator</td></tr>
<tr><td>Getting money out</td><td>Redeem from the game panel at 3x the load, capped at 8x, with ID and staff review</td><td>Withdrawal under the operator's terms and its regulator's rules</td></tr>
<tr><td>Published odds or RTP</td><td>None</td><td>Depends on the regulator and the operator</td></tr>
<tr><td>Minimum age</td><td>18+</td><td>Set by the regulator</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The right-hand column is deliberately general. Licensed casinos differ from one another and from one regulator to the next, and this page is not a guide to any of them.</p>

<h2>The legal model is the real difference</h2>
<p>A licensed online casino takes wagers under a license. The regulator that issued it decides where the casino can operate, what checks it must run and how complaints are handled. Casinova does not operate under that framework. It runs under a sweepstakes model, which is a different category, and it does not tell you that the model is permitted where you live. That is for you to confirm before you sign up.</p>
<p>Two posts go deeper on this: <a href="/blog/what-are-sweepstakes-games">what sweepstakes games are</a> and <a href="/blog/sweepstakes-vs-real-money-gambling">sweepstakes versus real-money gambling</a>. Neither is legal advice, and neither is this page.</p>

<h2>How the games differ</h2>
<p>On Casinova you do not play inside the Casinova website. You create a login for a third-party game app from your dashboard, load credits into it from your wallet, and play in the provider's app or web player. Eight games are live, including <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a>, <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a>, <a href="/games/vegas-sweeps">Vegas Sweeps</a> and <a href="/games/cash-machine">Cash Machine</a>. The formats will look familiar if you have used a casino site: slots, keno and fish shooters. If the shooter format is new to you, start with <a href="/blog/what-is-a-fish-table-game">what a fish table game is</a>.</p>
<p>Each game holds its own balance. Credits loaded into Juwa stay in Juwa until you redeem them from the Juwa panel; they do not move across to another game.</p>

<h2>How the money side differs</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>One payment method.</strong> Deposits are by card through a payment partner, and checkout happens on the partner's page. Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime and crypto are not offered. The <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">card deposit guide</a> shows each step.</li>
<li><strong>Loads have fixed limits.</strong> $5 minimum and $500 maximum per load, rounded to the nearest dollar.</li>
<li><strong>The bonus is tied to deposit order.</strong> Your first deposit is matched 100% and your second 50% when you load a game. There is nothing after the second, and there are no promo codes.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem has a threshold and a cap.</strong> A redeem opens when the in-game balance reaches 3x the load, and total redeems on a load are capped at 8x. A $20 load opens redeem at $60 in the game and caps at $160.</li>
<li><strong>Every redeem is reviewed.</strong> You need an approved government ID, and a staff member reviews the request. Casinova does not promise a payout time. See <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">how to redeem</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What is not published</h2>
<p>The game providers do not publish odds or RTP figures for these apps, and Casinova does not control or publish them either. If you see a payout percentage quoted for Juwa or Game Vault somewhere online, it did not come from the provider. Outcomes are based on chance, and no pattern or strategy changes that. The <a href="/blog/are-online-fish-table-games-safe">safety checklist</a> explains what you can and cannot verify about a game.</p>

<h2>Which one suits you</h2>
<p>This is not a case of one being better. If a regulator's oversight, a formal complaints route and published game information matter most to you, a licensed operator in a place where one is available is the fit, and Casinova is not a substitute for that. If you are specifically looking for app-style games such as Juwa or Game Vault behind one card-funded wallet with fixed load and redeem rules, that is what Casinova provides.</p>
<p>Either way, the same habits apply: decide your budget before you deposit, treat the money as spent on entertainment, and stop when it is gone. The <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a> lists tools and help lines.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Is Casinova Gaming a real online casino?</h3>
<p>No. It is a sweepstakes gaming platform and does not hold a casino license.</p>
<h3>Can I use Casinova where I live?</h3>
<p>Availability varies by jurisdiction and Casinova makes no legality claim for any location. Check the rules that apply to you before signing up. Players must be 18 or older.</p>
<h3>Do the games publish RTP like some casino games do?</h3>
<p>No. The providers do not publish odds or RTP for these apps, and Casinova does not either.</p>
<h3>Is redeeming the same as a casino withdrawal?</h3>
<p>Not quite. You redeem from the game panel once the in-game balance is at least 3x your load, up to an 8x cap, with an approved ID and a staff review. There is no promised payout time.</p>
<h3>Which payment methods does Casinova accept?</h3>
<p>Card only, through a payment partner. No other method is offered.</p>

<p><a href="/register?src=blog_casinovasgaming-vs-online-casinos&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=casinovasgaming-vs-online-casinos">Create your free account</a> and read the deposit and redeem screens yourself before you spend anything.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is for players 18+. Sweepstakes availability varies by jurisdiction; void where prohibited.</p>$t$,
