-- casinovasgaming-xp-leveling-explained
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Casinova XP and Levels Explained: VIP Points and Tiers$t$,
  excerpt = $t$Casinova Gaming does not have XP or numbered levels. Progress is measured in VIP points, and those points place you in one of four tiers: Bronze at 0, Silver at 500, Gold at 2,000 and Platinum at 5,000. Points come from card deposits, daily check-ins, the daily spin, completed game account requests and referrals.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>Casinova Gaming does not have XP or numbered levels. Progress is measured in VIP points, and those points place you in one of four tiers: Bronze at 0, Silver at 500, Gold at 2,000 and Platinum at 5,000. Points come from card deposits, daily check-ins, the daily spin, completed game account requests and referrals.</p>

<h2>XP versus VIP points</h2>
<p>If you searched for a Casinova XP curve or a level chart, there is not one. An earlier version of this page described an XP formula, level milestones and coin bonuses that the site does not have. The only progress number on your account is your VIP points total, and the only "levels" are the four VIP tiers. Everything below describes that system.</p>

<h2>The four tiers</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Points needed</th><th>Referral share</th><th>Daily spins</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Bronze</td><td>0</td><td>5%</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Silver</td><td>500</td><td>10%</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gold</td><td>2,000</td><td>15%</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Platinum</td><td>5,000</td><td>25%</td><td>3</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The referral share is a percentage of a referred friend's first deposit, credited to you. Daily spins are per 24 hours. The <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-vip-tiers-explained">VIP tiers guide</a> covers the support benefits attached to each tier, and the <a href="/vip">VIP page</a> shows the same table.</p>

<h2>Where points come from</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>VIP points</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Card deposit credited to your wallet</td><td>1 point per dollar, rounded to the nearest whole point</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily check-in on the Daily rewards page</td><td>5 on the first day, 1 more for each consecutive day, up to 11 from day seven</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily mission: spin the wheel, then claim</td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cash prize on the daily spin</td><td>10 points per dollar won, so 10 to 100</td></tr>
<tr><td>Game account request completed by staff</td><td>50</td></tr>
<tr><td>Friend signs up with your referral code</td><td>10</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A few details behind the table:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Deposits.</strong> Points are added when a card deposit is credited to your wallet. A $25 deposit is 25 points.</li>
<li><strong>Check-in streak.</strong> The Daily rewards page in your dashboard has a claim button. Day one pays 5 points, day two 6, and so on up to 11 on day seven and every day after. The day is counted in UTC. Miss one and the streak goes back to 5.</li>
<li><strong>Daily mission.</strong> After you take your <a href="/spin">daily spin</a>, return to Daily rewards and claim 5 more points. One claim per day.</li>
<li><strong>Spin prizes.</strong> The wheel pays $1, $2, $3, $4, $7 or $10, or nothing. A cash prize also adds 10 points per dollar, so a $3 result is 30 points. The <a href="/blog/daily-rewards-coins-guide">daily spin guide</a> explains the wheel.</li>
<li><strong>Game account requests.</strong> When a game account request is completed for you, 50 points are added.</li>
<li><strong>Referrals.</strong> 10 points for each friend who signs up with your code. See the <a href="/blog/referral-program-earn-coins">referral guide</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How long does Silver take?</h2>
<p>Silver is 500 points. Here is the arithmetic for a member who never deposits and never refers anyone, using the check-in and the mission only:</p>
<ul>
<li>First seven days of check-ins: 5 + 6 + 7 + 8 + 9 + 10 + 11 = 56 points.</li>
<li>Seven daily missions: 35 points. First week total: 91.</li>
<li>Each day after that: 11 for the check-in plus 5 for the mission, 16 points.</li>
</ul>
<p>At that pace 500 points takes about 33 days with no missed days, before counting any spin prizes. Deposits shorten it by one point per dollar and each referral by 10 points. Gold at 2,000 and Platinum at 5,000 are long-term totals on check-ins alone, which is why most of the points at those tiers come from deposits and referrals.</p>

<h2>What points and tiers do not change</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The deposit match.</strong> 100% on your first deposit and 50% on your second, at every tier. There is no tier multiplier on it. See the <a href="/blog/maximize-fish-table-bonus">deposit bonus guide</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Load limits.</strong> $5 to $500 per load for everyone.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem rules.</strong> Redeem opens at 3x the load and is capped at 8x, with an approved ID and a staff review, at every tier.</li>
<li><strong>Game results.</strong> Points are a Casinova account feature. They are not visible inside <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a>, <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a> or any other game, and they have no influence on outcomes, which are based on chance.</li>
</ul>
<p>Points cannot be spent, traded or redeemed. They only set your tier and your place on the <a href="/leaderboard">leaderboard</a>, which the <a href="/blog/casinovasgaming-leaderboard-guide">leaderboard guide</a> describes.</p>

<h2>Climbing without overspending</h2>
<p>The fastest way to add points is to deposit, because every dollar is a point. That is also the worst reason to deposit. A tier raises a referral percentage and adds a spin or two; it does not pay back money spent to reach it. Set your deposit budget from what you can afford to lose, let the points fall where they fall, and use the free sources, the check-in, the mission and the wheel, for the rest. If you notice yourself depositing to hit a threshold, take a break and read the <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a>.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Does Casinova Gaming have XP or levels?</h3>
<p>No. There is no XP and no level number. Accounts have a VIP points total and one of four tiers: Bronze, Silver, Gold or Platinum.</p>
<h3>What is the fastest free way to earn VIP points?</h3>
<p>Check in every day and claim the daily mission after your spin. With a full streak that is 16 points a day, plus 10 points per dollar of any spin prize.</p>
<h3>Do VIP points expire?</h3>
<p>Tiers follow your total points, and nothing in the program removes points for inactivity. Only the check-in streak resets if you miss a day.</p>
<h3>Can I exchange VIP points for credits or cash?</h3>
<p>No. Points only determine your tier and leaderboard rank.</p>
<h3>Does a higher tier improve the deposit bonus or redeem limits?</h3>
<p>No. The 100% and 50% deposit matches, the $5 to $500 load range and the 3x to 8x redeem rules are the same at every tier.</p>

<p><a href="/register?src=blog_casinovasgaming-xp-leveling-explained&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=casinovasgaming-xp-leveling-explained">Create your free account</a> and claim your first check-in on day one.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is for players 18+. Sweepstakes availability varies by jurisdiction; void where prohibited.</p>$t$,
