-- win-sweeps-vs-other-fish-table-platforms
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$How Casinova Gaming Differs From Other Fish Table Platforms$t$,
  excerpt = $t$Casinova Gaming differs from many fish table platforms in ways you can check yourself: deposits are by card only through a payment partner, the load and redeem rules are published and identical for every game, and every redeem requires an approved government ID and a staff review. This page lists what Casinova does, without rating any other operator, and gives you questions to ask any platform before you deposit.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>Casinova Gaming differs from many fish table platforms in ways you can check yourself: deposits are by card only through a payment partner, the load and redeem rules are published and identical for every game, and every redeem requires an approved government ID and a staff review. This page lists what Casinova does, without rating any other operator, and gives you questions to ask any platform before you deposit.</p>

<h2>Why this is not a ranking</h2>
<p>We cannot verify how other operators handle deposits, payouts or support, so we will not score them or name them. Comparison pages that do are usually guessing. What we can do is state our own rules precisely and show you where to confirm each one on the site. You can then hold any other platform to the same test.</p>

<h2>1. Card-only deposits through a payment partner</h2>
<p>At Casinova the only way to add money is the card checkout in your dashboard. The payment happens on the payment partner's page. Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime and crypto are not offered.</p>
<p>That has two practical effects. A card payment leaves a record with your card issuer, which a transfer to a personal payment handle does not. And it gives you a simple fraud test: any message asking you to pay another way in Casinova's name is not from Casinova. The <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">card deposit guide</a> shows the checkout step by step.</p>

<h2>2. Published load and redeem rules</h2>
<p>The numbers are the same for every live game and every VIP tier, and they are printed on each game page:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Casinova Gaming</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Minimum load</td><td>$5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Maximum load</td><td>$500</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deposit match</td><td>100% on the first deposit, 50% on the second, none after</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem opens at</td><td>3x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem cap</td><td>8x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem requirements</td><td>Approved government ID, staff review</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Knowing the threshold and the cap before you load means you can do the arithmetic in advance. A $10 load opens redeem at a $30 game balance and caps at $80. The <a href="/blog/deposit-amounts-and-limits-casinova">limits guide</a> and <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">how to redeem</a> go through more examples.</p>

<h2>3. ID review before any redeem</h2>
<p>Every redeem request is reviewed by a staff member, and the account must have an approved government photo ID. The review confirms the player is an adult and that the account belongs to one real person. It also means a redeem is not automatic and Casinova does not promise a payout time. We would rather say that plainly than advertise a speed we cannot stand behind. The <a href="/blog/casinova-id-verification-guide">ID verification guide</a> explains what to upload, and <a href="/blog/how-sweepstakes-payouts-work">how payouts work</a> covers what happens after approval.</p>

<h2>4. One wallet, and a clear line between live and coming soon</h2>
<p>One Casinova wallet funds every game. Each game has a panel where you create the login, load, check the balance and redeem. Eight games can be loaded today: <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a>, <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a>, <a href="/games/mr-all-in-one">MR All In One</a>, <a href="/games/cash-machine">Cash Machine</a>, <a href="/games/cash-frenzy">Cash Frenzy</a>, <a href="/games/vegas-sweeps">Vegas Sweeps</a>, <a href="/games/gameroom">Gameroom</a> and <a href="/games/mafia">Mafia</a>.</p>
<p>Six more are listed as coming soon and are not available: Orion Stars, Fire Kirin, Panda Master, Vblink, Milky Way and Ultrapanda. Their cards are marked "soon" and cannot be loaded. If one of those names brought you here, the <a href="/blog/fire-kirin-orion-stars-alternatives">coming-soon guide</a> points to the closest live game.</p>

<h2>5. Support inside your account</h2>
<p>Support runs through the chat on the site and the Messages inbox in your dashboard, 24/7. Because the conversation is tied to your account, staff can see your deposits, loads and redeem requests without asking you to prove who you are in a messaging app. The <a href="/support">support page</a> has the details.</p>

<h2>6. What Casinova does not claim</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>No odds or RTP figures.</strong> The providers do not publish them, so neither do we. Outcomes are based on chance.</li>
<li><strong>No promise of winning.</strong> No strategy, timing or game choice makes a result certain.</li>
<li><strong>No promo codes, free credits or no-deposit bonus.</strong> The deposit match and the daily spin are the offers.</li>
<li><strong>No legality claim.</strong> Casinova is a sweepstakes platform, not a licensed casino. Availability varies by jurisdiction and it is your job to check yours.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Questions to ask any fish table platform</h2>
<ol>
<li>How do I pay, and does the payment go to a business through a checkout or to a personal handle?</li>
<li>Are the minimum load, the bonus terms and the redeem threshold written down somewhere I can read before depositing?</li>
<li>Is there an ID check before a payout, and who reviews it?</li>
<li>Can I reach support from inside my account, and is there a record of the conversation?</li>
<li>Which games can I actually load today?</li>
<li>Does the site quote payout percentages, and if so, where do they come from?</li>
</ol>
