<li><strong>Play</strong> in the provider's app or web player.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem from the panel</strong> when the game balance is at least 3x the load. Total redeems are capped at 8x the load, you need an approved government ID, and staff review each request. There is no promised payout time. See <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">how to redeem</a>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>The redeem math for a fish session</h2>
<p>Take a $20 load. Redeem opens when the game balance shows $60 and the cap is $160. Below $60 the redeem button stays locked, so a session that ends at $45 is a balance to keep playing or leave in the game, not one to cash out. Knowing the two numbers before you start tells you when to stop: once you are above the threshold, every further shot is a choice to risk a redeemable balance.</p>

<h2>Session habits that matter more than aim</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Start at the lowest bet per shot.</strong> Fish tables can use credits fast because you can fire many shots a minute.</li>
<li><strong>Decide the load before you open the app</strong> and do not top up mid-session.</li>
<li><strong>Do not chase one large target.</strong> A big fish that has taken many shots is not "due". Each shot is independent.</li>
<li><strong>Set a time limit.</strong> Shared rooms keep going after you leave.</li>
</ul>
<p>New players may prefer to learn the panel on a slower format first; the <a href="/blog/best-fish-table-games-beginners">beginner ranking</a> explains why. Play is for adults 18 and over, and the <a href="/responsible-play">responsible play page</a> is there if a session stops being fun.</p>

