-- beginner-guide-fish-table-games
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$Fish Table Games for Beginners: Your First Session, Step by Step$t$,
  excerpt = $t$A fish table game is a shared shooting game: every shot costs a bet you set, and a fish pays a multiple of that bet if your shot takes it. As a beginner, learn three things first: the bet-per-shot control, how quickly a balance moves, and the load and redeem rules. Outcomes are decided by the game software, so plan a first session as entertainment with a fixed budget.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>A fish table game is a shared shooting game: every shot costs a bet you set, and a fish pays a multiple of that bet if your shot takes it. As a beginner, learn three things first: the bet-per-shot control, how quickly a balance moves, and the load and redeem rules. Outcomes are decided by the game software, so plan a first session as entertainment with a fixed budget.</p>

<h2>What you are looking at</h2>
<p>Fish tables look busy the first time you open one. Almost everything on screen falls into five groups:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Your cannon.</strong> One seat at the edge of the table. You aim it, typically by tapping or dragging, and it fires where you point.</li>
<li><strong>The bet control.</strong> Usually plus and minus buttons near the cannon. This number is what each shot costs. It is the most important control in the game.</li>
<li><strong>Your balance.</strong> Shown beside the cannon. It drops with every shot and rises when a fish is credited to you.</li>
<li><strong>The fish.</strong> Small ones are common and pay small multiples. Large ones and bosses are rare, pay more, and soak up many shots.</li>
<li><strong>Other players.</strong> Their cannons sit at the other seats and their shots land on the same fish. You share the room, but each balance is separate.</li>
</ul>
<p>Extras such as lock-on aiming, special weapons or bonus fish differ from one provider to the next, so learn them inside the game you pick. The format itself is covered in <a href="/blog/what-is-a-fish-table-game">what a fish table game is</a>, and the <a href="/blog/fish-table-glossary">glossary</a> defines the terms you will see.</p>

<h2>What you control and what you do not</h2>
<p>You choose the room, the bet per shot, the target, and when you leave. Those choices decide how long a balance lasts and how much of it is exposed at any moment.</p>
<p>You do not control whether a shot takes a fish. The software decides that, and the providers of the games on Casinova do not publish odds. Good aim keeps you from wasting shots on empty water. It does not turn a fish table into a game you can beat with practice, and anyone who tells you otherwise is guessing or selling something.</p>

<h2>Before your first session</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Create a Casinova account</strong> and confirm your email from the link we send.</li>
<li><strong>Upload your ID early.</strong> Redeem needs an approved government ID, and the <a href="/blog/casinova-id-verification-guide">ID guide</a> explains what to send. Doing it first means it is not the thing you wait on later.</li>
<li><strong>Deposit by card.</strong> Card is the only method. Casinova does not offer Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime or crypto. The <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">deposit guide</a> lists the amounts.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a live game that has fish tables.</strong> <a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a> is the fish specialist. <a href="/games/gameroom">Gameroom</a>, <a href="/games/mr-all-in-one">MR All In One</a>, <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a> and <a href="/games/vegas-sweeps">Vegas Sweeps</a> have fish alongside slots and keno.</li>
<li><strong>Create the game login</strong> from that game's page, then use Load to move $5 to $500 from your wallet into the game. The <a href="/blog/how-to-load-credits-from-wallet">load guide</a> walks through the panel.</li>
</ol>

<h2>The money rules, with beginner-sized numbers</h2>
<p>Your first deposit is matched 100% when you load a game, and your second 50%. Redeem opens when the game balance reaches 3x the load and is capped at 8x the load in total.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>First-deposit load</th><th>In the game after the match</th><th>Redeem opens at</th><th>Redeem cap</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>$5</td><td>$10</td><td>$15</td><td>$40</td></tr>
<tr><td>$10</td><td>$20</td><td>$30</td><td>$80</td></tr>
<tr><td>$20</td><td>$40</td><td>$60</td><td>$160</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A small load keeps the threshold small, which is what you want while you are still learning the controls. There are no promo codes, free credits or no-deposit bonuses at Casinova, so the deposit match is the whole offer. The <a href="/blog/maximize-fish-table-bonus">bonus guide</a> has the details.</p>

<h2>Your first session</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Write down two numbers.</strong> The balance at which you will submit a redeem (at least 3x your load) and the balance at which you will close the app.</li>
<li><strong>Open the lowest-stake room</strong> and set the bet per shot to the table minimum. Leave it there for the whole session.</li>
<li><strong>Spend the first few minutes watching.</strong> See how fast fish cross, how many shots a mid-size fish absorbs, and how quickly your balance moves at the minimum bet.</li>
<li><strong>Shoot fish you can finish.</strong> Small and mid-size fish that are well inside the table are better practice than a boss the whole room is firing at.</li>
<li><strong>Glance at the balance often.</strong> In a fish room it changes every second, and it is easy to lose track.</li>
<li><strong>Stop at one of your numbers.</strong> If you reach the redeem number, go back to the Casinova game page, use Check Balance, and submit the redeem. The <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">redeem guide</a> covers the review step.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Five beginner mistakes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Raising the bet to recover.</strong> A higher bet per shot empties a balance faster. It does not change your chances per shot.</li>
<li><strong>Chasing a boss across the screen.</strong> Shots at a fish that swims off before it is taken are simply spent.</li>
<li><strong>Holding the fire button down.</strong> Continuous fire at the minimum bet is still continuous spending. Pause between targets.</li>
<li><strong>Making a large first load.</strong> A $500 first load needs a $1,500 balance before redeem opens. Learn the game on a threshold you can see.</li>
<li><strong>Believing timing tips.</strong> Nobody outside the provider knows when a fish will pay. Our <a href="/blog/boss-fish-jackpot-timing-guide">boss fish and timing guide</a> explains why.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Where to go next</h2>
<p>If you are unsure whether you would rather shoot or spin, <a href="/blog/fish-table-vs-slots-which-is-better">fish table vs slots</a> compares the two, and <a href="/blog/best-fish-table-games-beginners">best games for beginners</a> ranks all eight live games by how easy they are to start. Once you know you like fish tables, <a href="/blog/best-fish-table-games-online">our fish table ranking</a> sorts the live games by how much fish play each one has.</p>
<p><a href="/register?src=blog_beginner-guide-fish-table-games&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=beginner-guide-fish-table-games">Create a free Casinova account</a> when you are ready, and keep the first load small.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes platform for players 18+, and availability varies by jurisdiction. Set a budget before you load, and use the limits and help on the <a href="/responsible-play">Responsible Play</a> page if a session stops being fun.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Are fish table games skill or chance?</h3>
<p>Both in a limited sense. You decide where to aim, how much each shot costs and when to stop, and those decisions affect how long a session lasts. Whether a shot takes a fish is decided by the game software, so no technique makes results predictable.</p>
<h3>How much do I need to start?</h3>
<p>The minimum load at Casinova is $5 and the maximum is $500 per load. On a first deposit, a $5 load is matched 100%, which puts $10 in the game and opens redeem at $15.</p>
<h3>Which Casinova game should a beginner open for fish tables?</h3>
<p>Juwa if you already know you want fish tables, because fish rooms are what that app is built around. If you want slots and keno to fall back on while you learn, MR All In One or Gameroom put all three behind one login.</p>
<h3>Can I practice for free first?</h3>
<p>No. Casinova does not offer free play, free credits or no-deposit bonuses. The lowest-cost way to try a fish table is a $5 load at the minimum bet in the lowest-stake room.</p>$t$,
