</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Web player or app download?</h2>
<p>Both lead to the same Game Vault lobby and both use the same login from your panel. The web player runs in a browser tab with nothing to install, which suits a quick session or a device where you would rather not add an app. The download is the provider's own app package. Our <a href="/blog/how-to-play-casinova-on-mobile">mobile guide</a> covers what to expect on Android and iPhone.</p>
<p>One safety habit matters here: reach the web player and the download through the buttons on the Casinova Game Vault page, not through search results or links sent in a message. Lookalike pages exist for popular game names, and a login typed into the wrong site is a login given away.</p>

<h2>Getting in for the first time</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Create a Casinova account</strong> and confirm your email.</li>
<li><strong>Open the Game Vault page and tap Create Account.</strong> In the panel, request your game login. The username and password appear under Your Account when the request completes. <a href="/blog/how-to-create-game-vault-account">How to create a Game Vault account</a> goes through every screen.</li>
<li><strong>Fund your wallet by card</strong> if it is empty. The <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">deposit guide</a> lists the amounts. Card is the only method; Casinova does not offer Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime or crypto.</li>
<li><strong>Load.</strong> Enter $5 to $500 on the Load tab. The panel shows what will arrive in the game, including any deposit match, before you confirm.</li>
<li><strong>Open the web player or app</strong> and sign in with the username and password from the panel.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Inside the lobby</h2>
<p>Game Vault's catalog is made up of slots, keno and fish games, with slots as the largest part. The provider rotates individual titles, so we do not print a list that would go stale. <a href="/blog/game-vault-all-games-breakdown">Game Vault explained</a> describes the three sections and who each suits. If fish tables are the reason you are here, compare it with the fish specialist in <a href="/blog/game-vault-vs-juwa">Game Vault vs Juwa</a>.</p>
<p>Results in every title are decided by the provider's software, and no payout percentage is published. Play at a bet size that lets your balance last, and decide before you load when you will stop.</p>

<h2>The Casinova terms for Game Vault</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Load range:</strong> $5 to $500 per load. Amounts round to the nearest dollar at load.</li>
<li><strong>Deposit match:</strong> 100% on your first deposit, 50% on your second, applied when you load. Nothing after that.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem:</strong> opens when your Game Vault balance is at least 3x the load and is capped at 8x the load in total. An approved government ID is required and staff review every request. We do not promise a payout time.</li>
</ul>
<p>Example: a $25 first-deposit load puts $50 into Game Vault. Redeem opens at $75 and the cap for that load is $200. These terms are the same for every live game at Casinova.</p>

<h2>Coming back for another session</h2>
<p>Your Game Vault login stays in the panel, and the dashboard's My Games page lists every game where you have an account with a link back to its panel. A sensible routine is: open the Game Vault page, tap Check Balance, load if you want to, then open the player. Before a redeem, Check Balance again so the panel is comparing against your real balance. The <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">redeem guide</a> covers the rest.</p>

<h2>If something does not work</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The web player rejects your login.</strong> Copy the username and password from the panel with the copy buttons instead of typing them, and make sure you are on the page opened by the Casinova button.</li>
<li><strong>Load is unavailable.</strong> You need a game login first, and at least $5 in your Total Deposit wallet.</li>
<li><strong>A request sits on pending.</strong> Recent activity shows its status. Message <a href="/support">support</a> if it does not move.</li>
<li><strong>Redeem will not submit.</strong> Either your ID is not approved yet, or your last checked balance is below 3x the load.</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="/register?src=blog_game-vault-online-guide&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=game-vault-online-guide">Create a free Casinova account</a> to set up your Game Vault login.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes platform for players 18+, and availability varies by jurisdiction. Set a budget before you load, and use the limits and help on the <a href="/responsible-play">Responsible Play</a> page if a session stops being fun.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Can I play Game Vault online without downloading anything?</h3>
<p>Yes. The Play Game Vault button on the Casinova game page opens the provider's web player in a browser tab. You sign in with the Game Vault login shown in your Casinova panel.</p>
<h3>Where do I get a Game Vault login?</h3>
<p>From the Game Vault page at Casinova. Tap Create Account, request the login in the panel, and the username and password appear there when the request completes. Creating the login is free.</p>
<h3>Do I deposit inside Game Vault?</h3>
<p>No. You deposit by card into your Casinova wallet, then use the Load tab on the Game Vault page to move $5 to $500 into the game.</p>
<h3>Is Game Vault the same on the web player and the app?</h3>
<p>Both open the same provider lobby with the same login and balance. The difference is only whether you install an app or use a browser tab.</p>$t$,
