-- how-to-create-game-vault-account
UPDATE public.blog_posts SET
  title = $t$How to Create a Game Vault Account at Casinova Gaming$t$,
  excerpt = $t$To create a Game Vault account at Casinova Gaming, register a free Casinova account, confirm your email, open the Game Vault page, tap Create Account and request the login in the panel. Your Game Vault username and password appear in that panel when the request completes. Creating the login is free; you only need funds in your wallet when you load credits.$t$,
  content = $t$<p>To create a Game Vault account at Casinova Gaming, register a free Casinova account, confirm your email, open the Game Vault page, tap Create Account and request the login in the panel. Your Game Vault username and password appear in that panel when the request completes. Creating the login is free; you only need funds in your wallet when you load credits.</p>

<h2>Two accounts, one after the other</h2>
<p>You end up with two logins, and it helps to keep them apart:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Your Casinova account</strong> (email and password) holds your wallet, your ID status and your game panels.</li>
<li><strong>Your Game Vault account</strong> (a game username and password) is what you type into the Game Vault app or web player. It is created for you from inside your Casinova account.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Step 1: register at Casinova</h2>
<p>On the Create Account page you can continue with Google or Facebook, or fill in the form:</p>
<ul>
<li>Full name</li>
<li>Email</li>
<li>Phone number, with your country selected</li>
<li>Password of at least 6 characters, entered twice</li>
<li>Government ID photo, optional at this stage (JPEG, PNG or WebP)</li>
<li>Referral code, optional</li>
</ul>
<p>The ID photo is optional when you sign up but an approved ID is required before your first redeem, so adding it now saves a step later. The <a href="/blog/casinova-id-verification-guide">ID verification guide</a> explains what is accepted. You must be 18 or older.</p>

<h2>Step 2: confirm your email</h2>
<p>After you submit the form, Casinova sends a confirmation link to your email address. Your account is not active until you click it. Clicking the link signs you in. If the link has expired, sign in with the same email and password and a fresh link is sent. Check your spam folder if nothing arrives.</p>

<h2>Step 3: open the Game Vault page and tap Create Account</h2>
<p>Go to the <a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault page</a> and tap Create Account. If you are not signed in, you are sent to the sign-in page first and returned to Game Vault afterward. The button takes you to the Game Vault Account panel on the same page.</p>

<h2>Step 4: request the login in the panel</h2>
<p>Under Your Account the panel says you have no account yet and offers two choices:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Create Account.</strong> Casinova generates the login for you. The panel previews the username before you tap. For Game Vault it is based on your name with a number on the end.</li>
<li><strong>Own login.</strong> Choose your own username and password. Each must be 7 to 13 characters, letters and numbers only, no symbols. If the username is already taken, it is adjusted so it stays unique.</li>
</ul>
<p>Either way there is no charge to your wallet.</p>

<h2>Step 5: wait for the login to appear</h2>
<p>The button changes to show that the account is being created, and the request is listed under Recent activity with its status. You do not need to tap again. When the request completes, the panel shows an Active badge with your Game Vault username and password, an eye icon to reveal the password, and copy buttons for both.</p>
<p>We do not quote a time for this step. If the panel reports that a request is taking longer than usual, it offers a Cancel link so you can try again, and <a href="/support">live chat</a> can check the request for you.</p>

<h2>Step 6: fund your wallet and load</h2>
<p>A new Game Vault login starts with no credits. To add them:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Deposit by card</strong> into your Total Deposit wallet, from the Deposit section on the game page or from your dashboard. Card is the only method. Casinova does not offer Cash App, Zelle, Venmo, PayPal, Chime or crypto. See the <a href="/blog/wallet-deposit-guide-casinovasgaming">deposit guide</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Open the Load tab</strong> in the Game Vault panel and enter an amount from $5 to $500. Amounts round to the nearest dollar.</li>
<li><strong>Read the preview.</strong> It states what will arrive in the game, including the match: 100% on your first deposit, 50% on your second, nothing after.</li>
<li><strong>Tap Load.</strong> The load appears under Recent activity.</li>
</ol>
<p>The <a href="/blog/how-to-load-credits-from-wallet">load guide</a> explains the preview line by line.</p>

<h2>Step 7: sign in to Game Vault</h2>
<p>Use Play Game Vault on the same page to open the provider's web player, or Download App for the provider's download page. Sign in with the username and password from your panel. The <a href="/blog/game-vault-online-guide">Game Vault online guide</a> compares the two ways in, and <a href="/blog/game-vault-all-games-breakdown">Game Vault explained</a> describes the lobby.</p>

<h2>What to know before you redeem</h2>
<p>Redeem opens when your Game Vault balance is at least 3x the load and is capped at 8x the load in total. A $20 first-deposit load puts $40 in the game, opens redeem at $60 and caps at $160. You need an approved government ID, every request is reviewed by staff, and we do not promise a payout time. Use Check Balance in the panel before you submit. Details are in the <a href="/blog/how-to-redeem-winnings-fast">redeem guide</a>.</p>

<h2>One Game Vault account per player</h2>
<p>Once you have a login, the panel's button becomes Replace Account. Replacing creates a new Game Vault login and stops showing the old one, and the panel asks you to confirm first. Do not use it as a fix for a forgotten password, since your password is already shown in the panel. If your current login still holds credits, redeem or speak to support before replacing it.</p>
<p><a href="/register?src=blog_how-to-create-game-vault-account&amp;utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=how-to-create-game-vault-account">Create your free Casinova account</a> and request your Game Vault login from the game page.</p>
<p>Casinova Gaming is a sweepstakes platform for players 18+, and availability varies by jurisdiction. Set a budget before you load, and use the limits and help on the <a href="/responsible-play">Responsible Play</a> page if a session stops being fun.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Is it free to create a Game Vault account?</h3>
<p>Yes. Registering at Casinova and requesting a Game Vault login are both free, and requesting the login does not charge your wallet. You pay only when you deposit by card and load credits.</p>
<h3>Do I have to deposit before I can create the Game Vault login?</h3>
<p>No. You can request the login with an empty wallet. You need at least $5 in your Total Deposit wallet to load the game.</p>
<h3>Can I choose my own Game Vault username and password?</h3>
<p>Yes. Tap Own login in the panel and enter a username and password of 7 to 13 letters and numbers each, with no symbols. If the username is taken, it is adjusted to stay unique.</p>
<h3>Where do I find my Game Vault login later?</h3>
<p>On the Game Vault page at Casinova, under Your Account, and through the My Games page in your dashboard, which links back to the panel.</p>
<h3>Do I need ID to create the account?</h3>
<p>Not to create it. An approved government ID is required before your first redeem, so uploading it at signup or soon after is the practical choice.</p>$t$,
