</ul>
<p>The previous version of this page described "galactic jackpots" and invited readers to sign up for Milky Way. Those details were not verifiable and the game is not open, so they have been removed.</p>

<h2>"Space" is a theme, not a game type</h2>
<p>Most categories in our game list tell you what you will be doing: Slots, Fish Game, Arcade. Milky Way's category, Space, tells you what the app looks like. The list describes it as space-themed slots and fish games. Underneath the theme those are the two standard formats:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Slots:</strong> you set a bet, spin, and the result is decided on each spin.</li>
<li><strong>Fish tables:</strong> you set a bet per shot and aim at targets in a shared room. See <a href="/blog/what-is-a-fish-table-game">what a fish table game is</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>So when you look for something to play in the meantime, there are two honest ways to match it: by content (slots plus fish) or by the appeal of a strongly themed lobby.</p>

<h2>Closest live games</h2>
<h3>By content: Game Vault</h3>
<p><a href="/games/game-vault">Game Vault</a> is the live game with the nearest mix. It is a vault-style lobby with a large slots and keno catalog and fish tables alongside. If Milky Way interested you for its slots with fish as a second option, this is the match. <a href="/blog/game-vault-all-games-breakdown">Game Vault explained</a> shows what is inside.</p>
<h3>By theme: Vegas Sweeps or Mafia</h3>
<p>No live game has a space theme. If a themed lobby is what you enjoy, two live games lean on theme: <a href="/games/vegas-sweeps">Vegas Sweeps</a> is styled after a Las Vegas casino floor with slots, keno and a fish section, and <a href="/games/mafia">Mafia</a> is a mob-themed slots and arcade app. <a href="/blog/game-vault-vs-vegas-sweeps">Game Vault vs Vegas Sweeps</a> compares the two slot-heavy lobbies.</p>
<h3>If the fish tables were the draw</h3>
<p><a href="/games/juwa">Juwa</a> is the fish specialist among the live games and a better fit than a slots-first lobby.</p>

<h2>Vblink status</h2>
<p>Vblink is in the same position as Milky Way: listed, coming soon, and not loadable, requestable or downloadable through Casinova. Our list files it under Arcade and describes it as an arcade-style app with fish games, slots and casino-style titles. The closest live game is <a href="/games/mr-all-in-one">MR All In One</a>, which puts slots, fish and keno behind one login; <a href="/games/gameroom">Gameroom</a>, the live game in the Arcade category, is the other option. As with Milky Way, no launch date is known.</p>

<h2>How loading will work once either game is live</h2>
<p>Nothing about the money side is specific to a game. These are the platform rules for every live game, and they will apply to Milky Way and Vblink when they open:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>What applies</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Deposit method</td><td>Card only, into one Casinova wallet</td></tr>
<tr><td>Load size</td><td>$5 minimum, $500 maximum per load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deposit match</td><td>100% on the first deposit, 50% on the second, none after, applied at load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem threshold</td><td>In-game balance at least 3x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redeem cap</td><td>8x the load</td></tr>
<tr><td>Checks</td><td>Approved government ID, staff review, no payout-time promise</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The match follows your deposit order, not the game, so there is nothing to save up for a particular launch. The <a href="/blog/maximize-fish-table-bonus">deposit bonus guide</a> and <a href="/blog/how-sweepstakes-payouts-work">how payouts work</a> go through the detail, and the <a href="/blog/fire-kirin-orion-stars-alternatives">coming-soon overview</a> lists all six waiting games.</p>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
